  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「アメリカグリ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%A2%E3%83%A1%E3%83%AA%E3%82%AB%E3%82%B0%E3%83%AA",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107256800,
      "text": "アメリカグリ は、アメリカ合衆国東海岸原産のブナ科の落葉高木。高さ最大 30m、幹の直径 3mに達する。果実は食用となり、材は堅いため昔から先住民が用いてきた。\n病害虫に弱いため、近年はクリ胴枯病によって危機に瀕している。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「American chestnut」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_chestnut",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1374800381,
      "text": "The American chestnut is a large, fast-growing deciduous tree of the beech family native to eastern North America. As is true of all species in the genus Castanea, the American chestnut produces burred fruit with edible nuts. The American chestnut was once common in the Appalachian Mountain range and was a dominant species in the oak-chestnut forest region of its central and southern range."
    }
